#: ../../about.rst:1
msgid "About this manual"
msgstr ""

#: ../../about.rst:4
msgid "This manual describes the implemented tool and its deliberate limits. The separate GDS project records proposals, decisions, and review history. A proposal's state is not changed by making its typography better."
msgstr ""

#: ../../about.rst:8
msgid "The organization follows a practical documentation pattern: learn with tutorials, understand with topic guides, act with practical tasks, and check details in reference pages. Internals explain the invariants and proofs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../about.rst:12
msgid "The prose favors small examples, named assumptions, and direct statements. The aim is an explanation that another person can test. The design uses restrained color, strong headings, serif reading text, and accessible navigation. It does not imitate an author's words or layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../about.rst:17
msgid "This project was created with ``guidedog quickstart`` and is built by Guidedog. RST holds the prose. Graphviz holds the diagrams. LaTeX math notation holds equations. Typst remains only where a PDF typesetting template is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../about.rst:21
msgid "Build evidence and qualification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../about.rst:24
msgid "Guidedog release 0.6.2 introduces typed Odin plugins for source, HTML, and assets, while keeping Pages as an independent publishing service. The release passed 176 integration tests, all 36 library and tool suites, AddressSanitizer checks, five-platform builds and smoke tests, and twelve large-manual builds across CPython, Django, and Flask. Diagnostic and link results matched their established baselines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../about.rst:30
msgid "Earlier publisher compatibility is no longer a release requirement. Qualification checks (via ``guidedog plugin check``) demonstrate interoperability across process boundaries; directly linked native callbacks remain trusted code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../about.rst:34
msgid "That evidence supports the released tool and its documented surface. It is not a claim of universal Sphinx equivalence or unbounded memory safety. See :doc:`compatibility` for the retained limits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../about.rst:38
msgid "Documentation maintenance commands are in :doc:`howto/maintain-docs`."
msgstr ""
